.TH EUCLID-CLI-EMM-LIST-BACKUPS 1 "October 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-emm-list-backups \- list the nightly backups the Euclid manager has written
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli
[\fB\-\-endpoint\fR \fIURL\fR]
.B emm list-backups
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lists the backup archives EMM has written to its backup directory,
newest first, together with how the nightly backup is set up. Takes no
arguments. The caller must be authenticated as an administrator; see
.BR euclid-cli-emm (1)
for how that's checked.
.PP
The list is read from the directory itself, not from a record the
backup keeps. A backup that dies part-way - killed by the kernel for
running out of memory, say - writes no log line and no record, but it
does leave its unzipped export behind. That file is listed too, with
.I complete
set to
.IR false ,
so a backup that fails every night shows up as a failure, not as a
quiet gap between dates.
.PP
The directory is the one on the host EMM runs on.
.PP
The JSON response is printed to standard output. It has:
.RS
.TP
.I directory
The backup directory
.RI ( euclid.modules.emm.backup.directory ).
.TP
.I enabled
Whether the nightly backup runs at all
.RI ( euclid.modules.emm.backup.enabled ).
.TP
.I schedule
Its cron expression, read in UTC
.RI ( euclid.modules.emm.backup.schedule ).
.TP
.I keep
How many archives retention keeps
.RI ( euclid.modules.emm.backup.keep ).
.TP
.I full
Whether the next backup takes the bulk data too (queue and topic
messages, object records) or only the configuration. Always
.I false
while a passphrase is set: an encrypted backup is built in memory, and
the bulk data is what doesn't fit.
.TP
.I encrypted
Whether a passphrase is configured
.RI ( euclid.modules.emm.backup.passphrase ).
Without one,
.I ekm
is left out of every backup.
.TP
.I backups
One object per file, newest first:
.RS
.TP
.I name ", " path
The file name, and the same with its directory.
.TP
.I startedAt
When the backup started, in UTC, read from the file name.
.TP
.I modified
When the file was last written. For a finished archive, roughly when
the backup ended.
.TP
.I size
Size in bytes.
.TP
.I complete
.I true
for a finished archive;
.I false
for an export that was never zipped - a backup running right now, or
one that died part-way. Retention never deletes these, so remove them
by hand once you're sure no backup is running.
.RE
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success,
.B 1
if the request fails or the caller is not an administrator.
.SH EXAMPLE
.PP
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 emm list-backups
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-emm (1),
.BR euclid-cli-emm-create-backup (1),
.BR euclid-cli-emm-export (1),
.BR euclid-cli-emm-import (1)
